    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.ThemeHighContrast">High contrast</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.ThemeHighContrastName">Use the high-contrast palette</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.ScanningTitle">Scanning</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.ScanningBody">Controls how much of each file Lumen reads for its content rules.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.MaxPrefix">Maximum content prefix per file</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.MaxPrefixName">Maximum megabytes inspected per file</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.SliderTooltip">1 to 16 MB</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.LoggingLabel">Write a local diagnostic log</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.LoggingBody">Technical events only. File contents, hashes and user names are never logged.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.TrayTitle">Window and tray</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.TrayBody">The tray icon is optional. Every action remains available in the main window.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.MinimizeToTrayLabel">Keep Lumen in the notification area</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.MinimizeToTrayBody">Closing or minimizing the window hides it instead of exiting. Use the tray menu to exit.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.MinimizeToTrayName">Minimize to tray and hide on close</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.TrayNotificationsLabel">Show scan notifications</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.TrayNotificationsBody">A small notification when a scan finishes while Lumen is hidden.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.TrayNotificationsName">Show scan notifications</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.RealtimeTitle">Real-time protection</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.RealtimeBody">While Lumen is open it re-checks new, changed and renamed files in your watched folders with the same documented rules used by on-demand scans. Files are only read; nothing is changed unless auto-quarantine is on.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.RealtimeLabel">Watch the configured folders</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.RealtimeName">Enable real-time protection</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.AutoQuarantineLabel">Quarantine matches automatically</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.AutoQuarantineBody">Matched files are moved into the encrypted vault without an extra prompt. With this off, Lumen only notifies you and never touches the file.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.AutoQuarantineName">Automatically quarantine real-time matches</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.RealtimeFootnote">This is a user-mode folder watcher, not a driver. It cannot see activity in system folders or outside your user profile, and it only runs while Lumen is open. Keep Microsoft Defender on.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.ReactivityTitle">How fast it reacts</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.ReactivityBody">Real-time protection waits a moment for a file to stop changing, then inspects it. More workers mean a faster answer on a busy folder.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.SettleDelayLabel">Wait before inspecting a changed file</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.SettleDelayBody">Short means a faster answer. Long means fewer half-written files are inspected.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.SettleDelayName">Settle delay before inspection</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.WorkerCountLabel">Files inspected at the same time</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.WorkerCountBody">More workers react faster but use more CPU. Three is a sensible default.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.WorkerCountName">Number of inspection workers</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.AutoKillName">Stop the process that is using a matched file</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.AutoKillLabel">Stop processes that are using a matched file</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.AutoKillBody">When a real-time match is found, Lumen can stop the processes whose executable or loaded module IS that file. System and protected processes are never stopped, and the file itself is never deleted. This needs the remediation switch above.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.AlertCooldownLabel">Repeat the alert for the same file</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.AlertCooldownBody">How long Lumen stays quiet about a file it has already reported. A longer silence means fewer interruptions.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.AlertCooldownName">Alert cooldown</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.AggressiveTitle">Aggressive mode</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.AggressiveBody">For a machine you are willing to watch closely. It adds the extra detection rules, watches the folders a dropper actually lands in (Downloads, Startup, temporary files), stops waiting before it inspects a new file, and can quarantine a high-confidence match without asking.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.AggressiveLabel">Turn on aggressive mode</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.AggressiveWarning">Aggressive mode catches more and reports more. Every extra rule is documented, but the extra rules are noisier than the standard ones, and watching more folders costs CPU. Turn it on when you are testing a suspicious download, and off again afterwards.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.AggressiveName">Aggressive mode</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.LanguageTitle">Language</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.LanguageBody">Choose the language of the interface. The change applies immediately, without a restart.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.LanguageEnglish">English</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.LanguageEnglishName">Use the English interface</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.LanguageFrench">Français</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.LanguageFrenchName">Use the French interface</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.WatchedTitle">Watched folders</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.WatchedBody">Extra folders the real-time monitor watches, in addition to the standard quick-scan folders. Paths that do not exist are ignored.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.ExcludedTitle">Excluded folders</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.ExcludedBody">Folders whose entire subtree the real-time monitor skips. Use this for build caches and tool directories that are noisy but harmless.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.AddFolder">Add folder…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.AddFolderName">Add a folder</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.RemoveFolder">Remove</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.RemoveFolderName">Remove this folder</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.NoWatched">Only the standard quick-scan folders are watched.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.NoExcluded">No folder is excluded.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.RemediationTitle">Remediation</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.RemediationBody">Let Lumen clean up a detection: stop the processes that use the file, remove the file permanently, and delete the autostart entries that point at it. Everything is presented as a plan that you confirm before anything happens.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.RemediationWarning">Warning: when this is on, Lumen can stop processes and delete files permanently. A file removed this way is not recoverable, except from the encrypted quarantine vault.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.RemediationLabel">Allow remediation actions</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.RemediationSwitchBody">Off by default. With this on, the Clean action appears on the Scan and Quarantine pages.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.RemediationName">Allow Lumen to stop processes and delete files</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.AlertTitle">Detection alert</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.AlertBody">Lumen can raise a full-screen alert when something is flagged, so a detection is never missed in a crowded window.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.AlertShowLabel">Show the detection alert</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.AlertShowBody">A window appears as soon as a file matches a rule.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.AlertShowName">Show the detection alert window</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.AlertSoundLabel">Play the alert sound</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Strings.Settings.AlertSoundBody">Off by default: an unexpected noise on someone's machine is rude.</sys:String>
